  "worked_solution": "First, we write the equation of our line in parametric form:\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{y}{2}=\\frac{z}{-1}=t\\,\u27f9\\,{\\begin{aligned}x=t \\\\ y=2t \\\\ z=-t,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nSubstituting the above expressions for $x$, $y$, and $z$ into the equation of the ellipsoid, we obtain:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{24}+\\frac{{z}^{2}}{2} & =1 \\\\ 8{x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+12{z}^{2} & =24 \\\\ 8(t)^{2}+(2t)^{2}+12(-t)^{2} & =24 \\\\ 8{t}^{2}+4{t}^{2}+12{t}^{2} & =24 \\\\ 24{t}^{2} & =24 \\\\ {t}^{2} & =1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, we get the solutions $t=-1$ and $t=1.$ \n\nNow, we substitute our solutions back into the equations of the line.\n\n- For $t=-1$, we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=-1 \\\\ y=2(-1)=-2 \\\\ z=-(-1)=1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the first point is $(-1,-2,1).$\n\n- For $t=1$, we have\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=1 \\\\ y=2(1)=2 \\\\ z=-1,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nso the second point is $(1,2,-1).$\n\nTherefore, the points of intersection are $(-1,-2,1)$ and $(1,2,-1).$",
